<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alidius Tjarda van Starkenborgh Stachouwer</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1888">1888</a>–<a href="/years/1978">1978</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alidius Tjarda van Starkenborgh Stachouwer was governor-general of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-indies">Dutch East Indies</a> from 1936, the last before the Japanese conquest. A conservative diplomat, he presided over a colony that rejected nationalist demands for autonomy such as the Soetardjo petition of 1936. He stayed at his post when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> invaded in 1942 and spent the rest of the war in Japanese internment. He later served as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> ambassador to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and representative to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nato">NATO</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alidius-tjarda-van-starkenborgh-stachouwer.jpg" alt="Alidius Tjarda van Starkenborgh Stachouwer" width="320" height="456" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Willem van de Poll · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Alidius_Warmoldus_Lambertus_Tjarda_van_Starkenborgh_Stachouwer_(1935).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
